    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/US-CA-Remote/Social-Work-Recruitment-and-Placement-Coordinator_R-2105": {
      "title": "Social Work Recruitment and Placement Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub   in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; Candidates must currently reside in California for consideration. &#xa;&#xa; ABOUT THE ROLE &#xa;&#xa;The grant-funded Social Work Recruitment and Placement Coordinator supports the administration of the California Social Work Education Capacity Expansion grant (SWECE) for the Master of Social Work program. The role focuses on outreach, recruitment, and student field placement in underserved California communities, in collaboration with Strategic Partnership Associates and Social Work faculty and staff. Works closely with the MSW Program Director and MSW Field Director to meet grant requirements and coordinate field placements.  Specifically, this position provides comprehensive support to students seeking field placement/supplemental supervision, field faculty, agency supervisors, directors and executive directors through implementation of placement procedures and policy. The position is grant funded and is anticipated to end by June 30, 2027.​​ TYPE OF SUPERVISION:     Receive ​ close supervision ​ from the ​ Program Director, MSW ​ .   ​ ​ Close Supervision — indicates that the incumbent is assigned duties according to specific procedures. Work is checked frequently , and in addition there may be formal training. ​     POSITION DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:      ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:     Percentage   ​ ​ Outreach & Recruitment   ​ Collaborate with Strategic Partnership team to perform outreach in underserved California communities, publicize the MSW program, and recruit students from underrepresented populations ​   Engage in targeted recruitment for field placement opportunities in students’ local communities supporting students in locating field sites.   ​ ​ 3 5 % ​   Field Placement Coordination & Student Support   ​ ​ Coordinate field placement process for students and ensure that applicable students are placed at appropriate field sites that satisfy the Field Program guidelines and HCAI grant’s criteria.   ​   Provide guidance to students in locating field sites. Serve as university liaison and representative around field placement inquiries from internal and external stakeholders.   Monitor field agencies to ensure proper supervision and task assignment to students in practicum roles.   Respond to field placement questions from students, site supervisors, and agency directors.    Troubleshoot student placement issues in coordination with the field director/assistant field director, field instructors, field practicum specialist and other university staff/faculty.    Inform students, directors of sites, and site supervisors about field policies, procedures and expectations.   35%   Field Agency Identification & Vetting   Identify and asses s agencies in underserved California communities to serve as field placement sites for MSW students.   T rack and maintain data on student intern placements by term in coordination with the Field Director     2 5 %   Perform other duties related to the SWECE grant , as assigned.   5 %   TOTAL   100%     POSITION SPECIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS:   EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, CERTIFICATION AND/OR LICENSES:   Master of Social Work degree from a CSWE-accredited MSW program   Prefer 2 + years post-master's experience placing MSW students for field practicum in a university online platform   Prefer some experience engaging in outreach or student recruitment events       ESSENTIAL KNOWL EDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES :    ​ ​   ​ Knowledge of academic processes in college/university setting.   ​ Excellent interpersonal and communications skills.   ​ Highly developed organizational skills and attention to detail.   ​ Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) or equivalent Google Workspace tools (Gmail, Docs, Sheets, Slides)   ​ Able to leverage AI-powered tools (e.g., Microsoft Copilot, Google Gemini, ChatGPT, Grammarly, or similar) to improve productivity, streamline communication, draft content, summarize information, and support day-to-day administrative tasks   ​ Ability to exercise independent judgment, demonstrate tact and diplomacy, and maintain a high level of confidentiality.   ​ Ability to problem solve , troubleshoot, and work under pressure.   ​ Ability to work effectively within a collaborative environment.   ​ Substantial experience in an academic environment is desired.   ​ ​     Machines, Tools, Equipment, Electronic Devices and Software :   ​ Strong competence in Microsoft Office is expected. Knowledge of SharePoint and Sonia is preferred. ​     Contact with Students:   ​ Frequent ​   Contact with Faculty and/or Staff:   ​ Frequent ​   Contact with Community and Vendors: ​ Frequent ​     SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:     Working conditions are generally normal for an office environment .  Position may be required to work flexible hours given the varied availabilities of field site agency personnel and other stakeholders . C alifornia residency is required, as  travel within California  is required approximately 1-4 times a year.   Applicants for this position are subject to a background check and a criminal history review .    The hiring range for this position is $25.00-$30.00 an hour . Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to geographical location, knowledge, skills, years BENEFITS AND PERKS   At the University of Massachusetts Global, we support your total well-being with flexible and meaningful benefits:   Health:  Medical, dental, and vision coverage with spending account options. Work-Life Balance : Remote options, flexible schedules, 1/2 day Fridays (biweekly), generous time off, including paid holidays and a paid winter break. Financial Security:  Life, disability, accident, legal, identity protection, and student debt support. Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option. 3% non-elective contribution and up to 6% match for a 9% total employer contribution! Education:  Tuition discounts for employees and family and Tuition Exchange program with other universities. PSLF eligible employer. Wellness:  Counseling services, Free Calm Health subscription and year-round wellness programs. &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
    },
    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/United-States-Remote/Adjunct-Faculty---Master-of-Social-Work--Remote-_R-2112": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Master of Social Work (Remote)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nPart time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; This position is open to candidates who currently reside in one of the following approved states from which the role may be performed remotely: Alabama, Arizona, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Virginia, Wisconsin. ABOUT THE ROLE School of Health and Behavioral Sciences Adjunct Faculty - Master of Social Work Position Overview:   This is a fully remote position that offers flexibility in scheduling but requires adherence to course deadlines and institutional policies. Remote adjuncts must have reliable internet access and a dedicated workspace to effectively manage teaching responsibilities. This role is ideal for experienced professionals seeking to contribute to higher education while maintaining the flexibility of remote work. Applicants will be hired to teach didactic and field education courses within the MSW programs.    Key Responsibilities: Teaching duties, mentoring, or supervising students. Delivering course content, engaging with students in discussion boards, and grading and providing detailed feedback on assignments. Collaborating with faculty or staff within the social work department including timely response to department emails. Utilizing specific technologies or tools (e.g., LMS, video platforms, field placement tracking software). Attending required meetings, training, or development sessions. If teaching field seminar, liaison with practicum agencies and supervisors on a regular basis to ensure student success in field practicum.     Required Qualifications: A Master of Social Work (MSW) degree from a CSWE-accredited program is required plus 2 year teaching experience in a university setting Available to hold synchronous sessions or supplemental supervision for MSW students across various time zones.     Preferred Qualifications: Online Teaching Experience (2 year or more) Field Seminar Instruction Experience (2 year or more) Experience supervising students in their field practicum and working with agency supervisors (1 year or more) Experience teaching in the following areas will be given preference: clinical social work, research methods, and field practicum Work Environment: A remote adjunct work environment is a flexible, virtual setting where instructors deliver course content, engage with students, and fulfill academic responsibilities from a remote location. This environment typically relies on digital communication tools, learning management systems (LMS), and virtual collaboration platforms to facilitate teaching and interaction. Compensation: The following salary range reflects compensation paid for a 3-unit course (101.25 hours) and varies based on the faculty member’s course assignment. 3-unit Lecture Course: The hiring range for this position is $3456.00 to $3856.00. Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to; geographical location, knowledge, skills, and experience. Application Process: To apply, please submit the following materials: Current resume or curriculum vitae (CV). Cover letter outlining your qualifications and interest in the role. Contact information for [number] professional references. [Any additional documentation such as transcripts, teaching evaluations, or certifications.] &#xa;&#xa; BENEFITS AND PERKS   Work-Life Balance : Remote options and flexible schedules Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option Education:  Tuition discounts &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
    },
    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/US-CA-Remote/Adjunct-Faculty---California-Multiple-Subject-Credential-MAT-Programs--Remote-_R-2098": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – California Multiple Subject Credential/MAT Programs (Remote)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nPart time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; This position is open to candidates who currently reside in California. ABOUT THE ROLE School of Education Adjunct Faculty – California Multiple Subject Credential/MAT Programs Position Overview: Adjunct faculty within the University of Massachusetts Global’s School of Education play a vital role in delivering high-quality, student-centered instruction in an online learning environment. They bring real-world expertise and a commitment to fostering academic excellence for future educators and leaders. Adjunct instructors must be willing to engage with faculty, students, and other stakeholders to ensure well-rounded, rigorous learning experiences that offer students the highest levels of support. This position requires a California teaching credential and current California K-8 public school teaching experience. Key Responsibilities: Responsibility 1: Teaching duties, mentoring, or supervising students. Responsibility 2: Preparing and delivering course content or assessments. Responsibility 3: Collaborating with faculty or staff for curriculum planning. Responsibility 4: Utilizing specific technologies or tools (e.g., LMS, video platforms). Responsibility 5: Attending required meetings, training, or development sessions. Responsibility 6: Holding virtual, weekly, open office hours for students. Responsibility 7: Engaging in program review and assessment activities as needed. Responsibility 8: Participating in calibration meetings relating to PLOs, CLOs, and Professional Dispositions Required Qualifications: Master’s Degree or Higher in Education, Teaching and/or, Related Field California (CA) Clear Multiple Subject/CLAD Credential Minimum 5 years teaching experience in a California (K-8) schools.  Experience teaching diverse student populations. Experience using educational technology Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in education or an educational related field. CA Administrative Credential. Experience teaching in higher education (online, hybrid) Trained assessor of or extensive knowledge of CalTPAs. Experience mentoring or supervising students or candidates. Experience using specific educational tools such as Go React and Rise Modules. Resides in the state of California. Work Environment: A remote adjunct work environment is a flexible, virtual setting where instructors deliver course content, engage with students, and fulfill academic responsibilities from a remote location. This environment typically relies on digital communication tools, learning management systems (LMS), and virtual collaboration platforms to facilitate teaching and interaction. Compensation: This course pays 23.17 per hour Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to; geographical location, knowledge, skills, and experience. Application Process: To apply, please submit the following materials: Current resume or curriculum vitae (CV). Cover letter outlining your qualifications and interest in the role. Contact information for 2 professional references. [Any additional documentation such as transcripts, teaching evaluations, or certifications.] The position will remain posted until 12/3/2026 or until a sufficient pool of qualified applicants has been reached, whichever occurs first. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis, and interested candidates are encouraged to apply early to ensure full consideration. The university reserves the right to close the posting prior to the stated date once an adequate applicant pool has been established. &#xa;&#xa; BENEFITS AND PERKS   Work-Life Balance : Remote options and flexible schedules Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option Education:  Tuition discounts &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
