    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/United-States-Remote/Admission-Service-Representative_R-2120": {
      "title": "Admission Service Representative",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nFull time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub   in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; This position is open to candidates who currently reside in one of the following approved states from which the role may be performed remotely: Alabama, Arizona, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Virginia, Wisconsin. &#xa;&#xa; ABOUT THE ROLE &#xa;&#xa;Under general direction from the Admissions Supervisor, the Admission Service Representative is responsible for the processing of applications in administrative computing system. The Admission Representative is responsible for successfully guiding the applicant through the admissions process and for representing UMass Global in a positive and professional manner. TYPE OF SUPERVISION RECEIVED:   General direction from the Admissions Supervisor POSITION DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:               Essential functions:  100% of time Process applications in administrative computing system Prepare files for evaluation/decision.  Link scanned documents in document imaging system. Create and update files. Track received documents in computing system, enter transfer coursework. Input communication codes, status codes, and trigger correspondence Provide support and assistance to both applicants and University stakeholders Assist applicants with troubleshooting issues as related to policies and procedures Assist in the development of training materials university stakeholders Assist with the training of university student teams Run audit reports on application data and follow up with University campus staff Assist with quality control reporting and data integrity Responsible for maintaining regular contact with university partners, particularly the Enrollment Coaches, via regular scheduled meetings, and data report follow-up Assist in the updating and review of applications and forms Assist with testing new procedures and processes Other duties as assigned Non-Essential Functions of the Job: May require work hours outside of standard business hours. POSITION SPECIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS: Special Conditions of Employment:  Position may be required to work flexible hours particularly given campuses’ extended hours of operation, and may require occasional weekend and/or evening work.  All applicants are subject to a background check and criminal history review.  Working conditions are normal for an office environment. Knowledge, Education and Experience: At least 1 year experience working in an Admission or Registrar office in a Higher Education Institution or equivalent work experience Knowledge and experience with administrative computing and document imaging systems, preferably Banner,  SoftDocs, Argos, Raptor, and Salesforce Knowledge of Admission policies and procedures Desired Qualifications: Ability to perform accurate and efficient entry of data into administrative software Adequate typing skills to complete data entry requests in a timely manner Ability to prioritize duties when faced with interruptions, distractions and fluctuating workload and completing them in a timely manner Communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact with diverse individuals and groups at all organizational levels, both inside and outside of the university Ability to organize and handle large quantity of work with accuracy and efficiency Ability to use tact and diplomacy and maintain a high level of confidentiality Knowledge of basic arithmetic computations Strong commitment to teamwork and customer service Machines, Tools, Equipment, Electronic Devices and Software:   Ability to use standard office equipment, including PC, phone, copier, and calculator Computer skills in the use of word processing and electronic mail, preferably of Microsoft Word and Outlook. Ability to learn new computer applications and administrative software.  Document Imaging software Contact with Students:   Daily. Contact with Faculty and/or Staff:   Daily Contact with Community and Vendors: Occasional The hiring range for this position is $17.00 - $21.50 per hour . Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to geographical location, knowledge, skills, years & depth of experience, and equity with internal team members. &#xa;&#xa; BENEFITS AND PERKS   At the University of Massachusetts Global, we support your total well-being with flexible and meaningful benefits:   Health:  Medical, dental, and vision coverage with spending account options. Work-Life Balance : Remote options, flexible schedules, 1/2 day Fridays (biweekly), generous time off, including paid holidays and a paid winter break. Financial Security:  Life, disability, accident, legal, identity protection, and student debt support. Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option. 3% non-elective contribution and up to 6% match for a 9% total employer contribution! Education:  Tuition discounts for employees and family and Tuition Exchange program with other universities. PSLF eligible employer. Wellness:  Counseling services, Free Calm Health subscription and year-round wellness programs. &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
