    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/United-States-Remote/Full-Time-Faculty-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Legal-Studies_R-2118": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty Assistant or Associate Professor Legal Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub   in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; This position is open to candidates who currently reside in one of the following approved states from which the role may be performed remotely: Alabama, Arizona, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Virginia, Wisconsin.     In order to collaborate with nationally distributed colleagues. Employees must be available for collaboration during core hours from 9am to 2pm (PST). &#xa;&#xa; ABOUT THE ROLE &#xa;&#xa;UMass Global invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the School of Arts and Sciences, supporting the Legal Studies portfolio. In keeping with the University’s mission to provide an accessible, inclusive, and transformative education grounded in excellence and flexibility, faculty are hired for their recognized expertise in their field of discipline and are expected to work as self-directed professionals who advance student success and the University’s strategic goals. Faculty will serve on a 12-month contract, with rank determined by prior academic and professional experience and the needs of the University. The position operates within a culture of academic freedom, intellectual inquiry, and respect for diverse perspectives, and faculty are expected to model the University’s core values of innovation, service, integrity, collaboration, respect, and inclusion. All faculty fulfill the University’s Core Responsibilities and Expectations and adhere to the Faculty Constitution & Bylaws and Faculty Manual. Workloads also include one or more of the following areas: curriculum and teaching, which may include teaching paced and/or self-paced courses, course management, and the design, development, and continuous improvement of curriculum; mentoring, which involves guiding and supporting the growth of students, staff, and fellow faculty; and service, which may include participation in faculty governance, program maintenance and development, accreditation and assessment activities, and other work that strengthens the University and its communities. Program-specific duties may include teaching across the core legal studies curriculum, such as legal research and writing, civil litigation, contracts, torts, legal ethics, and business law. Faculty may also teach or mentor students in the Legal Studies Capstone. Where assigned, they also support program review, the legal studies advisory board, and outreach to the legal community. The successful candidate will collaborate effectively across programs and schools, show openness to new ideas and respect for differing views, and uphold the highest standards of professional ethics in relationships with students and colleagues. TYPE OF SUPERVISION:   Receive general supervision from the School Associate Dean. General Supervision — indicates that the incumbent performs a variety of duties; some of which may be complex duties within established policy guidelines; and receives occasional supervision. POSITION DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:    ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:     Teaching   Teach an assigned load of online courses (paced and/or self-paced), as agreed in the annual faculty workload.  Support student learning through timely, substantive engagement, clear communication, and constructive feedback.  Evaluate student work fairly and consistently against academic standards and course learning outcomes.  Foster free inquiry and an inclusive, respectful learning environment for adult learners.  Apply professional development and assessment findings to strengthen teaching practice.    Curriculum Management and Development   Collaborate with internal stakeholders to maintain the quality and currency of an assigned curriculum portfolio, keeping courses aligned with program learning outcomes, workforce and industry needs, and applicable accreditation or licensure standards.  Design, develop, and revise courses in collaboration with instructional design, program, and assessment teams.  Serve as course manager for assigned courses, coordinating course readiness, updates, and consistency across sections.  Use course and program assessment findings to inform curriculum decisions and continuous improvement.    Academic Leadership and Student Mentoring (as assigned)   Provide program leadership where assigned, such as program management, coordination, and support for programmatic accreditation requirements.  Coordinate, support, and mentor adjunct faculty to promote instructional quality and consistency.    Professional Development   Complete purposeful professional development, identified in the annual workload plan and connected to the faculty member’s role and growth needs. Focus areas may include disciplinary knowledge and professional currency; teaching practice; curriculum design, development, and assessment; leadership, communication, and collaboration; and developments in higher education relevant to our students and institutional model.    Service and Other Duties   Contribute to the institution through faculty governance, committee work, and school and University initiatives.  Contribute to the discipline or profession through activities such as engagement with professional organizations, or participation in role-related conferences. Perform other duties and projects as assigned, consistent with the faculty role and as agreed in the annual workload.    POSITION SPECIFICATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS: EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, CERTIFICATION AND/OR LICENSES: Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an ABA-accredited law school, or an earned doctorate in a related discipline from an institutionally accredited institution Active license to practice law, in good standing, in at least one U.S. jurisdiction. Recent legal practice experience. Minimum of 3 years experience teaching in an online higher education institution. Demonstrated expertise in developing and delivering current, market-relevant, and engaging curriculum, assessments, and learning activities in an online-first LMS.  Involvement in related professional and academic associations.  ESSENTIAL KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES:  Strong organizational, communication, and collaboration skills. Experience working in a remote environment. Evidence of scholarly, professional, or community engagement activities. Demonstrated ability to manage, support, and train adjuncts in an online environment.  Commitment to student-centered teaching and supporting a diverse adult learner population Experience applying data-informed approaches to enhance student success and retention.  Ability to engage collegially and collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and professionals across disciplines.  Committed to cultivating a workplace culture grounded in respect, openness, and constructive dialogue.  Machines, Tools, Equipment, Electronic Devices, and Software: Extensive experience in using webinar and virtual meeting platforms; Microsoft Office (PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook); Salesforce CRM; social media platforms; collaboration and project management tools. Contact with Students: Frequent Contact with Faculty and/or Staff: Frequent Contact with Community and Vendors: Occasional SPECIAL REQUIREMENT:  All applicants are subject to a background check and criminal history review.  Incumbents are expected to travel 5-10% of the time to network with professional associations and partners and to attend conferences in support of the University’s mission and the faculty member’s professional growth. COMPENSATION: The hiring range for this position is $105,000 to $120,000 annually. Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to geographical location, knowledge, skills, years & depth of experience, and equity with internal team members . &#xa;&#xa; BENEFITS AND PERKS   At the University of Massachusetts Global, we support your total well-being with flexible and meaningful benefits:   Health:  Medical, dental, and vision coverage with spending account options. Work-Life Balance : Remote options, flexible schedules, generous time off, including paid holidays and a paid winter break. Financial Security:  Life, disability, accident, legal, identity protection, and student debt support. Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option. 3% non-elective contribution and up to 6% match for a 9% total employer contribution! Education:  Tuition discounts for employees and family and Tuition Exchange program with other universities. PSLF eligible employer. Wellness:  Counseling services, Free Calm Health subscription and year-round wellness programs.   &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
    },
    "https://umassglobal.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UMassGlobalCareers/job/United-States-Remote/Adjunct-Faculty-Single-Subject-MAT-Program---Core-Methods-Courses--Math--Science--Art--Music--English---Remote-_R-2121": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Single Subject/MAT Program – Core Methods Courses (Math, Science, Art, Music, English) (Remote)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nPart time\n\nPlease Note: Internal Employees, please access the Jobs Hub in Workday to apply for the position. ABOUT US   University of Massachusetts Global is a private, nonprofit affiliate of the University of Massachusetts, created to help working adults change their lives through flexible, high-quality education built for real life. Regionally accredited by the WASC Senior College and University Commission (WSCUC) and recognized by U.S. News & World Report  among the Best Online Programs for 13 consecutive years (2013–2025), the university has a long track record of online innovation. Students across 49 states and internationally can upskill, reskill, and move forward without putting life on hold through technology-enabled, real-world learning.​ With 55+fully online, career-focused programs designed around the realities of work, family, and constant change, we remain ever-focused on developing future-ready learners who can thrive in a rapidly shifting world.   &#xa;&#xa; This position is open to candidates who currently reside in one of the following approved states from which the role may be performed remotely: Alabama, Arizona, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Virginia, Wisconsin. ABOUT THE ROLE School of Education Adjunct Faculty-Single Subject/MAT Program – Core Methods Courses (Math, Science, Art, Music, English) Position Overview: Adjunct faculty within the University of Massachusetts Global’s School of Education play a vital role in delivering high-quality, student-centered instruction in an online learning environment. They bring real-world expertise and a commitment to fostering academic excellence for future educators and leaders. Adjunct instructors must be willing to engage with faculty, students, and other stakeholders to ensure well-rounded, rigorous learning experiences that offer students the highest levels of support. This position requires a California teaching credential and current California 6-12 public school teaching experience. Key Responsibilities: Responsibility 1: Teaching duties, mentoring, or supervising students. Responsibility 2: Preparing and delivering course content or assessments. Responsibility 3: Collaborating with faculty or staff for curriculum planning. Responsibility 4: Utilizing specific technologies or tools (e.g., LMS, video platforms). Responsibility 5: Attending required meetings, training, or development sessions. Responsibility 6: Holding virtual, weekly, open office hours for students. Responsibility 7: Engaging in program review and assessment activities as needed. Responsibility 8: Participating in calibration meetings relating to PLOs, CLOs, and Professional Dispositions Required Qualifications: Master’s Degree or Higher in Education, Teaching and/or, Related Field California (CA) Clear Multiple Subject Credential Minimum 5 years teaching experience in a California secondary (6-12) school. Experience teaching diverse student populations. Experience using educational technology. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in education or an educational related field. CA Administrative Credential. Experience teaching in higher education (online, hybrid) Trained assessor of or extensive knowledge of CalTPAs. Experience mentoring or supervising students or candidates. Experience using specific educational tools for observation such as Go React and Rise Modules. Resides in the state of California. Work Environment: A remote adjunct work environment is a flexible, virtual setting where instructors deliver course content, engage with students, and fulfill academic responsibilities from a remote location. This environment typically relies on digital communication tools, learning management systems (LMS), and virtual collaboration platforms to facilitate teaching and interaction. Compensation: The following salary range reflects compensation paid for a 3-unit course (101.25 hours) and varies based on the faculty member’s course assignment. 3-unit Lecture Course: The hiring range for this position is $3456.00 to $3856.00. Offers are determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to; geographical location, knowledge, skills, and experience. Application Process: To apply, please submit the following materials: Current resume or curriculum vitae (CV) Cover letter outlining your qualifications and interest in the role Copy of California Teaching and/or Administration Credentials Unofficial copy of transcripts from your highest completed degree Contact information for 3 professional references The position will remain posted until 12/10/2026 or until a sufficient pool of qualified applicants has been reached, whichever occurs first. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis, and interested candidates are encouraged to apply early to ensure full consideration. The university reserves the right to close the posting prior to the stated date once an adequate applicant pool has been established. &#xa;&#xa; BENEFITS AND PERKS   Work-Life Balance : Remote options and flexible schedules Retirement:  403(b) plan with a Roth option Education:  Tuition discounts &#xa;&#xa; Equal Employment Opportunity – UMass Global is committed to providing an educational and work environment free of unlawful discrimination and harassment in any form. UMass Global prohibits all forms of discrimination and harassment on the basis of  age, race (including hairstyle/texture, protective hairstyles, braids, locks, and twists), color, religion (including religious observance, belief, practice dress and grooming practices), citizenship, pregnancy (including temporary physical or mental limitations related to, affected by, or arising out of pregnancy, childbirth, or any related medical conditions), sex, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, national origin, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, legally-protected medical condition, military (past, present or prospective) status, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, sexual and reproductive health, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by local, State or Federal law.   Reasonable Accommodation – UMass Global provides reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities. If you need a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process, please notify the recruitment department at recruiting@umassglobal.edu."
    }
  },
